3. No resale of the tool

You may not sell, resell, rent, lease, or license for a fee the Software or a
Modified Version, or charge for its download, installation package, distribution
or a license to use it as a reusable tool. This restriction applies to standalone
copies and to inclusion in a paid software bundle, skill collection, template
library or other product. Renaming it, making modifications, or describing the
charge as access, membership or a subscription does not permit charging for
copies or licenses to the Software itself.

A fee for creating, designing, editing or delivering Presentation Outputs is
expressly permitted under section 4. Charging for that work is not resale of the
Software. Free sharing under section 2 remains permitted. Any broader permission
to sell or license the tool requires a separate written agreement from Daniel
Mansz. This license creates no separate general ban on hosting or automation;
any distribution or licensing of the Software must still comply with this section.

4. Presentation Outputs and paid client work

You may create Presentation Outputs without charge from Daniel Mansz, charge
clients for your presentation work, and use, publish, sell or deliver the resulting
Presentation Outputs for personal or commercial purposes. You may deliver the
PDF, HTML and editable project together, and clients may open, present, share,
edit and continue working on their presentations.

This permission expressly includes distributing the rendering code, styles,
viewer, catalogue, layouts and other Software components included by the workflow
in a real Presentation Output, including when you are paid for that presentation.
The embedded or bundled Software remains under this license; recipients may use
it under these same terms. Delivering a real presentation does not grant a right
to extract, market or sell the Software as a reusable tool or template product.
Merely wrapping the skill or a reusable template library in a nominal presentation
does not turn a sale of the tool into permitted presentation work.

Daniel Mansz claims no rights under this license to your original presentation
content, your original additions, or your clients' material. No visible Slidebaby
logo, watermark, author credit or link is required on presentation slides or PDFs.
Retain existing legal notices in any Software code distributed with an output;
those notices may remain in source code, embedded notice data or accompanying
license files rather than appearing on slides.

